# A guard. For two hours the records of pending blocks outlived the block of the text in which they were made while a loop was being built twice. A snapshot that is put back lays them back whole while edges stay in kept code, so a record counted no arrival at a block that edges led to: the start of the copy for the rest was called unreachable, never begun, and the build stopped: the walk is over and an edge leads to a block that has no end.
